<li about="#cite_note-25" id="cite_note-25" data-mw-footnote-number="25"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwC2Y"><a href="#cite_ref-25" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwC2c"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC2g">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-25" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt85" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC2k" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite report ","href":"./Template:Cite_report"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"Reliable Digital Communications Using Unreliable Network Repeater Nodes"},"first":{"wt":"Paul"},"last":{"wt":"Baran"},"page":{"wt":"1"},"date":{"wt":"May 27, 1960"},"publisher":{"wt":"The RAND Corporation"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.rand.org/content/dam/rand/pubs/papers/2008/P1995.pdf"},"access-date":{"wt":"July 25, 2012"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFBaran1960" class="citation report cs1" about="#mwt85">Baran, Paul (May 27, 1960). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.rand.org/content/dam/rand/pubs/papers/2008/P1995.pdf" class="external text" id="mwC2o">Reliable Digital Communications Using Unreliable Network Repeater Nodes</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwC2s">(PDF)</span> (Report). The RAND Corporation. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwC2w"> </span>1<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwC20">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwC24">July 25,</span> 2012</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=report&amp;rft.btitle=Reliable+Digital+Communications+Using+Unreliable+Network+Repeater+Nodes&amp;rft.pages=1&amp;rft.pub=The+RAND+Corporation&amp;rft.date=1960-05-27&amp;rft.aulast=Baran&amp;rft.aufirst=Paul&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.rand.org%2Fcontent%2Fdam%2Frand%2Fpubs%2Fpapers%2F2008%2FP1995.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt85" id="mwC28"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-26" id="cite_note-26" data-mw-footnote-number="26"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwC3A"><a href="#cite_ref-26" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwC3E"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC3I">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-26" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt88" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC3M" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"About Rand"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.rand.org/about/history/baran.html"},"access-date":{"wt":"July 25, 2012"},"work":{"wt":"Paul Baran and the Origins of the Internet"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt88" id="mwC3Q"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.rand.org/about/history/baran.html" class="external text" id="mwC3U">"About Rand"</a>. <i id="mwC3Y">Paul Baran and the Origins of the Internet</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwC3c">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwC3g">July 25,</span> 2012</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Paul+Baran+and+the+Origins+of+the+Internet&amp;rft.atitle=About+Rand&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.rand.org%2Fabout%2Fhistory%2Fbaran.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt88" id="mwC3k"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Pelkey6.1a-27" id="cite_note-Pelkey6.1a-27" data-mw-footnote-number="27"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwC3o"><a href="#cite_ref-Pelkey6.1a_27-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwC3s"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC3w">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pelkey6.1a-27" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt91" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC30" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Pelkey"},"first":{"wt":"James L."},"title":{"wt":"Entrepreneurial Capitalism and Innovation: A History of Computer Communications 1968–1988"},"chapter":{"wt":"6.1 The Communications Subnet: BBN 1969"},"quote":{"wt":"As Kahn recalls: ... Paul Baran’s contributions ... I also think Paul was motivated almost entirely by voice considerations. If you look at what he wrote, he was talking about switches that were low-cost electronics. The idea of putting powerful computers in these locations hadn’t quite occurred to him as being cost effective. So the idea of computer switches was missing. The whole notion of protocols didn’t exist at that time. And the idea of computer-to-computer communications was really a secondary concern."},"chapter-url":{"wt":"https://historyofcomputercommunications.info/section/6.1/the-communications-subnet-bbn-1969/"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFPelkey" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt91">Pelkey, James L. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://historyofcomputercommunications.info/section/6.1/the-communications-subnet-bbn-1969/" class="external text" id="mwC34">"6.1 The Communications Subnet: BBN 1969"</a>. <i id="mwC38">Entrepreneurial Capitalism and Innovation: A History of Computer Communications 1968–1988</i>. <q id="mwC4A">As Kahn recalls: ... Paul Baran's contributions ... I also think Paul was motivated almost entirely by voice considerations. If you look at what he wrote, he was talking about switches that were low-cost electronics. The idea of putting powerful computers in these locations hadn't quite occurred to him as being cost effective. So the idea of computer switches was missing. The whole notion of protocols didn't exist at that time. And the idea of computer-to-computer communications was really a secondary concern.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=6.1+The+Communications+Subnet%3A+BBN+1969&amp;rft.btitle=Entrepreneurial+Capitalism+and+Innovation%3A+A+History+of+Computer+Communications+1968%E2%80%931988&amp;rft.aulast=Pelkey&amp;rft.aufirst=James+L.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fhistoryofcomputercommunications.info%2Fsection%2F6.1%2Fthe-communications-subnet-bbn-1969%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt91" id="mwC4E"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-28" id="cite_note-28" data-mw-footnote-number="28"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwC4I"><a href="#cite_ref-28" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwC4M"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC4Q">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-28" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt94" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC4U" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Barber"},"first1":{"wt":"Derek"},"date":{"wt":"Spring 1993"},"title":{"wt":"The Origins of Packet Switching"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.cs.man.ac.uk/CCS/res/res05.htm#f"},"journal":{"wt":"The Bulletin of the Computer Conservation Society"},"issue":{"wt":"5"},"issn":{"wt":"0958-7403"},"access-date":{"wt":"6 September 2017"},"quote":{"wt":"There had been a paper written by [Paul Baran] from the Rand Corporation which, in a sense, foreshadowed packet switching in a way for speech networks and voice networks"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFBarber1993" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt94">Barber, Derek (Spring 1993). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.cs.man.ac.uk/CCS/res/res05.htm#f" class="external text" id="mwC4Y">"The Origins of Packet Switching"</a>. <i id="mwC4c">The Bulletin of the Computer Conservation Society</i> (5). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC4g">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwC4k"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0958-7403" class="external text" id="mwC4o">0958-7403</a><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwC4s">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwC4w">September 6,</span> 2017</span>. <q id="mwC40">There had been a paper written by [Paul Baran] from the Rand Corporation which, in a sense, foreshadowed packet switching in a way for speech networks and voice networks</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Bulletin+of+the+Computer+Conservation+Society&amp;rft.atitle=The+Origins+of+Packet+Switching&amp;rft.ssn=spring&amp;rft.issue=5&amp;rft.date=1993&amp;rft.issn=0958-7403&amp;rft.aulast=Barber&amp;rft.aufirst=Derek&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.cs.man.ac.uk%2FCCS%2Fres%2Fres05.htm%23f&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt94" id="mwC44"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:5a2-29" id="cite_note-:5a2-29" data-mw-footnote-number="29"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwC48"><a href="#cite_ref-:5a2_29-0" id="mwC5A"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC5E">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-:5a2_29-1" id="mwC5I"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC5M">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:5a2-29" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt97" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC5Q" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Waldrop"},"first":{"wt":"M. Mitchell"},"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=eRnBEAAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PT285"},"title":{"wt":"The Dream Machine"},"date":{"wt":"2018"},"publisher":{"wt":"Stripe Press"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-1-953953-36-0"},"pages":{"wt":"286"},"language":{"wt":"en"},"quote":{"wt":"Baran had put more emphasis on digital voice communications than on computer communications."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFWaldrop2018" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt97">Waldrop, M. Mitchell (2018). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=eRnBEAAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PT285" class="external text" id="mwC5U"><i id="mwC5Y">The Dream Machine</i></a>. Stripe Press. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwC5c"> </span>286. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC5g">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwC5k"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-1-953953-36-0" title="Special:BookSources/978-1-953953-36-0" id="mwC5o"><bdi id="mwC5s">978-1-953953-36-0</bdi></a>. <q id="mwC5w">Baran had put more emphasis on digital voice communications than on computer communications.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=The+Dream+Machine&amp;rft.pages=286&amp;rft.pub=Stripe+Press&amp;rft.date=2018&amp;rft.isbn=978-1-953953-36-0&amp;rft.aulast=Waldrop&amp;rft.aufirst=M.+Mitchell&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3DeRnBEAAAQBAJ%26pg%3DPT285&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt97" id="mwC50"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-30" id="cite_note-30" data-mw-footnote-number="30"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwC54"><a href="#cite_ref-30" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwC58"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC6A">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-30" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt100" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC6E" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"On packet switching"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.nethistory.info/Archives/packets.html"},"access-date":{"wt":"2024-01-08"},"website":{"wt":"Net History"},"quote":{"wt":"[Scantlebury said] Clearly Donald and Paul Baran had independently come to a similar idea albeit for different purposes. Paul for a survivable voice/telex network, ours for a high-speed computer network."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt100" id="mwC6I"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nethistory.info/Archives/packets.html" class="external text" id="mwC6M">"On packet switching"</a>. <i id="mwC6Q">Net History</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwC6U">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwC6Y">January 8,</span> 2024</span>. <q id="mwC6c">[Scantlebury said] Clearly Donald and Paul Baran had independently come to a similar idea albeit for different purposes. Paul for a survivable voice/telex network, ours for a high-speed computer network.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Net+History&amp;rft.atitle=On+packet+switching&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nethistory.info%2FArchives%2Fpackets.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt100" id="mwC6g"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Pelkey6.1a2-31" id="cite_note-Pelkey6.1a2-31" data-mw-footnote-number="31"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwC6k"><a href="#cite_ref-Pelkey6.1a2_31-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwC6o"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC6s">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pelkey6.1a2-31" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt104" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC6w" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Pelkey"},"first":{"wt":"James L."},"title":{"wt":"Entrepreneurial Capitalism and Innovation: A History of Computer Communications 1968–1988"},"chapter":{"wt":"6.1 The Communications Subnet: BBN 1969"},"quote":{"wt":"As Kahn recalls: ... Paul Baran’s contributions ... I also think Paul was motivated almost entirely by voice considerations. If you look at what he wrote, he was talking about switches that were low-cost electronics. The idea of putting powerful computers in these locations hadn’t quite occurred to him as being cost effective. So the idea of computer switches was missing. The whole notion of protocols didn’t exist at that time. And the idea of computer-to-computer communications was really a secondary concern."},"chapter-url":{"wt":"https://historyofcomputercommunications.info/section/6.1/the-communications-subnet-bbn-1969/"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwC60" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt104" data-x-id="CITEREFPelkey">Pelkey, James L. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://historyofcomputercommunications.info/section/6.1/the-communications-subnet-bbn-1969/" class="external text" id="mwC64">"6.1 The Communications Subnet: BBN 1969"</a>. <i id="mwC68">Entrepreneurial Capitalism and Innovation: A History of Computer Communications 1968–1988</i>. <q id="mwC7A">As Kahn recalls: ... Paul Baran's contributions ... I also think Paul was motivated almost entirely by voice considerations. If you look at what he wrote, he was talking about switches that were low-cost electronics. The idea of putting powerful computers in these locations hadn't quite occurred to him as being cost effective. So the idea of computer switches was missing. The whole notion of protocols didn't exist at that time. And the idea of computer-to-computer communications was really a secondary concern.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=6.1+The+Communications+Subnet%3A+BBN+1969&amp;rft.btitle=Entrepreneurial+Capitalism+and+Innovation%3A+A+History+of+Computer+Communications+1968%E2%80%931988&amp;rft.aulast=Pelkey&amp;rft.aufirst=James+L.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fhistoryofcomputercommunications.info%2Fsection%2F6.1%2Fthe-communications-subnet-bbn-1969%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt104" id="mwC7E"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-32" id="cite_note-32" data-mw-footnote-number="32"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwC7I"><a href="#cite_ref-32" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwC7M"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC7Q">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-32" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt107" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC7U" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Kleinrock"},"first":{"wt":"L."},"date":{"wt":"1978"},"title":{"wt":"Principles and lessons in packet communications"},"journal":{"wt":"Proceedings of the IEEE"},"volume":{"wt":"66"},"issue":{"wt":"11"},"pages":{"wt":"1320–1329"},"bibcode":{"wt":"1978IEEEP..66.1320K"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1109/PROC.1978.11143"},"issn":{"wt":"0018-9219"},"quote":{"wt":"Paul Baran ... focused on the routing procedures and on the survivability of distributed communication systems in a hostile  environment, but did not concentrate on the need for resource sharing in its form as we now understand it; indeed, the concept of a software switch was not present in his work."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFKleinrock1978" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt107">Kleinrock, L. (1978). "Principles and lessons in packet communications". <i id="mwC7Y">Proceedings of the IEEE</i>. <b id="mwC7c">66</b> (11): <span class="nowrap" id="mwC7g">1320–</span>1329. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibcode_(identifier)" title="Bibcode (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC7k">Bibcode</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1978IEEEP..66.1320K" class="external text" id="mwC7o">1978IEEEP..66.1320K</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC7s">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1109%2FPROC.1978.11143" class="external text" id="mwC7w">10.1109/PROC.1978.11143</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC70">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwC74"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0018-9219" class="external text" id="mwC78">0018-9219</a>. <q id="mwC8A">Paul Baran ... focused on the routing procedures and on the survivability of distributed communication systems in a hostile  environment, but did not concentrate on the need for resource sharing in its form as we now understand it; indeed, the concept of a software switch was not present in his work.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Proceedings+of+the+IEEE&amp;rft.atitle=Principles+and+lessons+in+packet+communications&amp;rft.volume=66&amp;rft.issue=11&amp;rft.pages=1320-1329&amp;rft.date=1978&amp;rft.issn=0018-9219&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1109%2FPROC.1978.11143&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F1978IEEEP..66.1320K&amp;rft.aulast=Kleinrock&amp;rft.aufirst=L.&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt107" id="mwC8E"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-33" id="cite_note-33" data-mw-footnote-number="33"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwC8I"><a href="#cite_ref-33" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwC8M"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwC8Q">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-33" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt110" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwC8U" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite magazine ","href":"./Template:Cite_magazine"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Metz"},"first":{"wt":"Cade"},"date":{"wt":"3 September 2012"},"title":{"wt":"What Do the H-Bomb and the Internet Have in Common? Paul Baran"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.wired.com/2012/09/what-do-the-h-bomb-and-the-internet-have-in-common-paul-baran/"},"magazine":{"wt":"WIRED"},"quote":{"wt":"He was very conscious of people mistaken belief that the work he did at RAND somehow led to the creation of the ARPAnet. It didn&apos;t, and he was very honest about that."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFMetz2012" class="citation magazine cs1" about="#mwt110">Metz, Cade (September 3, 2012). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.wired.com/2012/09/what-do-the-h-bomb-and-the-internet-have-in-common-paul-baran/" class="external text" id="mwC8Y">"What Do the H-Bomb and the Internet Have in Common? Paul Baran"</a>. <i id="mwC8c">WIRED</i>. <q id="mwC8g">He was very conscious of people mistaken belief that the work he did at RAND somehow led to the creation of the ARPAnet. It didn't, and he was very honest about that.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=WIRED&amp;rft.atitle=What+Do+the+H-Bomb+and+the+Internet+Have+in+Common%3F+Paul+Baran&amp;rft.date=2012-09-03&amp;rft.aulast=Metz&amp;rft.aufirst=Cade&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.wired.com%2F2012%2F09%2Fwhat-do-the-h-bomb-and-the-internet-have-in-common-paul-baran%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt110" id="mwC8k"></span></span></li>
