<li about="#cite_note-Roberts1995-40" id="cite_note-Roberts1995-40" data-mw-footnote-number="40"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDCQ"><a href="#cite_ref-Roberts1995_40-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDCU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDCY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Roberts1995-40" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt136" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDCc" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Roberts"},"first1":{"wt":"Dr. Lawrence G."},"title":{"wt":"The ARPANET &amp; Computer Networks"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.packet.cc/files/arpanet-computernet.html"},"access-date":{"wt":"13 April 2016"},"date":{"wt":"May 1995"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20160324032800/http://www.packet.cc/files/arpanet-computernet.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"March 24, 2016"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRoberts1995" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt136">Roberts, Dr. Lawrence G. (May 1995). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20160324032800/http://www.packet.cc/files/arpanet-computernet.html" class="external text" id="mwDCg">"The ARPANET &amp; Computer Networks"</a>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.packet.cc/files/arpanet-computernet.html" class="external text" id="mwDCk">the original</a> on March 24, 2016<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDCo">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDCs">April 13,</span> 2016</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=The+ARPANET+%26+Computer+Networks&amp;rft.date=1995-05&amp;rft.aulast=Roberts&amp;rft.aufirst=Dr.+Lawrence+G.&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.packet.cc%2Ffiles%2Farpanet-computernet.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt136" id="mwDCw"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-41" id="cite_note-41" data-mw-footnote-number="41"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDC0"><a href="#cite_ref-41" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDC4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDC8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-41" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt139" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDDA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Edmondson-Yurkanan"},"first":{"wt":"Chris"},"date":{"wt":"2007"},"title":{"wt":"SIGCOMM&apos;s archaeological journey into networking&apos;s past"},"url":{"wt":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/1230819.1230840"},"journal":{"wt":"Communications of the ACM"},"language":{"wt":"en"},"volume":{"wt":"50"},"issue":{"wt":"5"},"pages":{"wt":"63–68"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1145/1230819.1230840"},"issn":{"wt":"0001-0782"},"quote":{"wt":"In his first draft dated Nov. 10, 1965 [5], Davies forecast today’s “killer app” for his new communication service:  “The greatest traffic could only come if the public used this means for everyday purposes such as shopping... People sending enquiries and placing orders for goods of all kinds will make up a large section of the traffic... Business use of the telephone may be reduced by the growth of the kind of service we contemplate.”"},"url-access":{"wt":"subscription"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFEdmondson-Yurkanan2007" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt139">Edmondson-Yurkanan, Chris (2007). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwDDE"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/1230819.1230840" class="external text" id="mwDDI">"SIGCOMM's archaeological journey into networking's past"</a></span>. <i id="mwDDM">Communications of the ACM</i>. <b id="mwDDQ">50</b> (5): <span class="nowrap" id="mwDDU">63–</span>68. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDDY">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1145%2F1230819.1230840" class="external text" id="mwDDc">10.1145/1230819.1230840</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDDg">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDDk"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0001-0782" class="external text" id="mwDDo">0001-0782</a>. <q id="mwDDs">In his first draft dated Nov. 10, 1965 [5], Davies forecast today's "killer app" for his new communication service:  "The greatest traffic could only come if the public used this means for everyday purposes such as shopping... People sending enquiries and placing orders for goods of all kinds will make up a large section of the traffic... Business use of the telephone may be reduced by the growth of the kind of service we contemplate."<span class="cs1-kern-right" id="mwDDw"></span></q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Communications+of+the+ACM&amp;rft.atitle=SIGCOMM%27s+archaeological+journey+into+networking%27s+past&amp;rft.volume=50&amp;rft.issue=5&amp;rft.pages=63-68&amp;rft.date=2007&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1145%2F1230819.1230840&amp;rft.issn=0001-0782&amp;rft.aulast=Edmondson-Yurkanan&amp;rft.aufirst=Chris&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdl.acm.org%2Fdoi%2F10.1145%2F1230819.1230840&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt139" id="mwDD0"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-42" id="cite_note-42" data-mw-footnote-number="42"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDD4"><a href="#cite_ref-42" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDD8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDEA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-42" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt142" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDEE" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Davies"},"first":{"wt":"D. W."},"date":{"wt":"1966"},"title":{"wt":"Proposal for a Digital Communication Network"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.dcs.gla.ac.uk/~wpc/grcs/Davies05.pdf"},"quote":{"wt":"Computer developments in the distant future might result in one type of network being able to carry speech and digital messages efficiently."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFDavies1966" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt142">Davies, D. W. (1966). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.dcs.gla.ac.uk/~wpc/grcs/Davies05.pdf" class="external text" id="mwDEI">"Proposal for a Digital Communication Network"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwDEM">(PDF)</span>. <q id="mwDEQ">Computer developments in the distant future might result in one type of network being able to carry speech and digital messages efficiently.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Proposal+for+a+Digital+Communication+Network&amp;rft.date=1966&amp;rft.aulast=Davies&amp;rft.aufirst=D.+W.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.dcs.gla.ac.uk%2F~wpc%2Fgrcs%2FDavies05.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt142" id="mwDEU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-43" id="cite_note-43" data-mw-footnote-number="43"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDEY"><a href="#cite_ref-43" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDEc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDEg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-43" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt145" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDEk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Roberts"},"first1":{"wt":"Dr. Lawrence G."},"title":{"wt":"The ARPANET &amp; Computer Networks"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.packet.cc/files/arpanet-computernet.html"},"access-date":{"wt":"13 April 2016"},"date":{"wt":"May 1995"},"quote":{"wt":"Then in June 1966, Davies wrote a second internal paper, \"Proposal for a Digital Communication Network\" In which he coined the word packet,- a small sub part of the message the user wants to send, and also introduced the concept of an \"Interface computer\" to sit between the user equipment and the packet network."},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20160324032800/http://www.packet.cc/files/arpanet-computernet.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"March 24, 2016"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwDEo" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt145" data-x-id="CITEREFRoberts1995">Roberts, Dr. Lawrence G. (May 1995). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20160324032800/http://www.packet.cc/files/arpanet-computernet.html" class="external text" id="mwDEs">"The ARPANET &amp; Computer Networks"</a>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.packet.cc/files/arpanet-computernet.html" class="external text" id="mwDEw">the original</a> on March 24, 2016<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDE0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDE4">April 13,</span> 2016</span>. <q id="mwDE8">Then in June 1966, Davies wrote a second internal paper, "Proposal for a Digital Communication Network" In which he coined the word packet,- a small sub part of the message the user wants to send, and also introduced the concept of an "Interface computer" to sit between the user equipment and the packet network.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=The+ARPANET+%26+Computer+Networks&amp;rft.date=1995-05&amp;rft.aulast=Roberts&amp;rft.aufirst=Dr.+Lawrence+G.&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.packet.cc%2Ffiles%2Farpanet-computernet.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt145" id="mwDFA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-K.G._Coffman_&amp;_A.M._Odlyzco-44" id="cite_note-K.G._Coffman_&amp;_A.M._Odlyzco-44" data-mw-footnote-number="44"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDFE"><a href="#cite_ref-K.G._Coffman_&amp;_A.M._Odlyzco_44-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDFI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDFM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-K.G._Coffman_&amp;_A.M._Odlyzco-44" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt148" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDFQ" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=TXhWJcsO134C&amp;q=ARPANET&amp;pg=PA29"},"author":{"wt":"K.G. Coffman &amp; A.M. Odlyzco"},"title":{"wt":"Optical Fiber Telecommunications IV-B: Systems and Impairments"},"publisher":{"wt":"[[Academic Press]]"},"pages":{"wt":"1022 pages"},"series":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;Optics and Photonics&apos;&apos; (edited by I. Kaminow &amp; T. Li)"},"access-date":{"wt":"2015-08-15"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-12-395173-1"},"date":{"wt":"2002-05-22"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFK.G._Coffman_&amp;_A.M._Odlyzco2002" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt148">K.G. Coffman &amp; A.M. Odlyzco (May 22, 2002). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=TXhWJcsO134C&amp;q=ARPANET&amp;pg=PA29" class="external text" id="mwDFU"><i id="mwDFY">Optical Fiber Telecommunications IV-B: Systems and Impairments</i></a>. <i id="mwDFc">Optics and Photonics</i> (edited by I. Kaminow &amp; T. Li). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academic_Press" title="Academic Press" id="mwDFg">Academic Press</a>. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDFk"> </span>1022 pages. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDFo">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDFs"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-12-395173-1" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-12-395173-1" id="mwDFw"><bdi id="mwDF0">978-0-12-395173-1</bdi></a><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDF4">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDF8">August 15,</span> 2015</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Optical+Fiber+Telecommunications+IV-B%3A+Systems+and+Impairments&amp;rft.series=%27%27Optics+and+Photonics%27%27+%28edited+by+I.+Kaminow+%26+T.+Li%29&amp;rft.pages=1022+pages&amp;rft.pub=Academic+Press&amp;rft.date=2002-05-22&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-12-395173-1&amp;rft.au=K.G.+Coffman+%26+A.M.+Odlyzco&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3DTXhWJcsO134C%26q%3DARPANET%26pg%3DPA29&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt148" id="mwDGA"></span></span></li>
