<li about="#cite_note-57" id="cite_note-57" data-mw-footnote-number="57"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDPM"><a href="#cite_ref-57" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDPQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDPU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-57" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt190" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDPY" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Copeland"},"first":{"wt":"B. Jack"},"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=YhQZnczOS7kC&amp;pg=PA349"},"title":{"wt":"Alan Turing&apos;s Electronic Brain: The Struggle to Build the ACE, the World&apos;s Fastest Computer"},"date":{"wt":"2012-05-24"},"publisher":{"wt":"OUP Oxford"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-19-960915-4"},"page":{"wt":"275"},"language":{"wt":"en"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFCopeland2012" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt190">Copeland, B. Jack (May 24, 2012). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=YhQZnczOS7kC&amp;pg=PA349" class="external text" id="mwDPc"><i id="mwDPg">Alan Turing's Electronic Brain: The Struggle to Build the ACE, the World's Fastest Computer</i></a>. OUP Oxford. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDPk"> </span>275. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDPo">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDPs"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-19-960915-4" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-19-960915-4" id="mwDPw"><bdi id="mwDP0">978-0-19-960915-4</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Alan+Turing%27s+Electronic+Brain%3A+The+Struggle+to+Build+the+ACE%2C+the+World%27s+Fastest+Computer&amp;rft.pages=275&amp;rft.pub=OUP+Oxford&amp;rft.date=2012-05-24&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-19-960915-4&amp;rft.aulast=Copeland&amp;rft.aufirst=B.+Jack&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3DYhQZnczOS7kC%26pg%3DPA349&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt190" id="mwDP4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:82-58" id="cite_note-:82-58" data-mw-footnote-number="58"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDP8"><a href="#cite_ref-:82_58-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDQA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDQE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:82-58" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt194" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDQI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite thesis ","href":"./Template:Cite_thesis"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Clarke"},"first":{"wt":"Peter"},"title":{"wt":"Packet and circuit-switched data networks"},"date":{"wt":"1982"},"degree":{"wt":"PhD"},"publisher":{"wt":"Department of Electrical Engineering, Imperial College of Science and Technology, University of London"},"url":{"wt":"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/bitstream/10044/1/35864/2/Clarke-PN-1982-PhD-Thesis.pdf"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFClarke1982" class="citation thesis cs1" about="#mwt194">Clarke, Peter (1982). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/bitstream/10044/1/35864/2/Clarke-PN-1982-PhD-Thesis.pdf" class="external text" id="mwDQM"><i id="mwDQQ">Packet and circuit-switched data networks</i></a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwDQU">(PDF)</span> (PhD thesis). Department of Electrical Engineering, Imperial College of Science and Technology, University of London.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Adissertation&amp;rft.title=Packet+and+circuit-switched+data+networks&amp;rft.degree=PhD&amp;rft.inst=Department+of+Electrical+Engineering%2C+Imperial+College+of+Science+and+Technology%2C+University+of+London&amp;rft.date=1982&amp;rft.aulast=Clarke&amp;rft.aufirst=Peter&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fspiral.imperial.ac.uk%2Fbitstream%2F10044%2F1%2F35864%2F2%2FClarke-PN-1982-PhD-Thesis.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt194" id="mwDQY"></span> "As well as the packet switched network actually built at NPL for communication between their local computing facilities, some simulation experiments have been performed on larger networks. A summary of this work is reported in [69]. The work was carried out to investigate networks of a size capable of providing data communications facilities to most of the U.K. ... Experiments were then carried out using a method of flow control devised by Davies [70] called 'isarithmic' flow control. ... The simulation work carried out at NPL has, in many respects, been more realistic than most of the ARPA network theoretical studies."</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Pelkey-59" id="cite_note-Pelkey-59" data-mw-footnote-number="59"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDQc"><a href="#cite_ref-Pelkey_59-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDQg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDQk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pelkey-59" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt197" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDQo" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"chapter-url":{"wt":"http://www.historyofcomputercommunications.info/Book/6/6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html"},"title":{"wt":"Entrepreneurial Capitalism and Innovation: A History of Computer Communications 1968–1988"},"last":{"wt":"Pelkey"},"first":{"wt":"James"},"chapter":{"wt":"6.3 CYCLADES Network and Louis Pouzin 1971–1972"},"access-date":{"wt":"February 3, 2020"},"archive-date":{"wt":"June 17, 2021"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210617093154/https://www.historyofcomputercommunications.info/Book/6/6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html"},"url-status":{"wt":"dead"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwDQs" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt197" data-x-id="CITEREFPelkey">Pelkey, James. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20210617093154/https://www.historyofcomputercommunications.info/Book/6/6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html" class="external text" id="mwDQw">"6.3 CYCLADES Network and Louis Pouzin 1971–1972"</a>. <i id="mwDQ0">Entrepreneurial Capitalism and Innovation: A History of Computer Communications 1968–1988</i>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.historyofcomputercommunications.info/Book/6/6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html" class="external text" id="mwDQ4">the original</a> on June 17, 2021<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDQ8">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDRA">February 3,</span> 2020</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=6.3+CYCLADES+Network+and+Louis+Pouzin+1971%E2%80%931972&amp;rft.btitle=Entrepreneurial+Capitalism+and+Innovation%3A+A+History+of+Computer+Communications+1968%E2%80%931988&amp;rft.aulast=Pelkey&amp;rft.aufirst=James&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.historyofcomputercommunications.info%2FBook%2F6%2F6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt197" id="mwDRE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-60" id="cite_note-60" data-mw-footnote-number="60"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDRI"><a href="#cite_ref-60" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDRM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDRQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-60" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#CITEREFHafnerLyon1998" about="#mwt203" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwDRU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"harvnb","href":"./Template:Harvnb"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Hafner"},"2":{"wt":"Lyon"},"3":{"wt":"1998"},"pages":{"wt":"39–41"}},"i":0}}]}'>Hafner <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDRY">&amp;</span> Lyon 1998</a><span about="#mwt203" id="mwDRc">, pp.</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt203" id="mwDRg"> </span><span about="#mwt203" id="mwDRk">39–41</span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Markoff_1999-61" id="cite_note-Markoff_1999-61" data-mw-footnote-number="61"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDRo"><a href="#cite_ref-Markoff_1999_61-0" id="mwDRs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDRw">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Markoff_1999_61-1" id="mwDR0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDR4">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Markoff_1999-61" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt209" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwDR8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFMarkoff1999" class="citation news cs1">Markoff, John (December 20, 1999). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://archive.nytimes.com/www.nytimes.com/library/tech/99/12/biztech/articles/122099outlook-bobb.html" class="external text" id="mwDSA">"An Internet Pioneer Ponders the Next Revolution"</a>. <i id="mwDSE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times" title="The New York Times" id="mwDSI">The New York Times</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20050304045456/http://partners.nytimes.com/library/tech/99/12/biztech/articles/122099outlook-bobb.html" class="external text" id="mwDSM">Archived</a> from the original on March 4, 2005<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDSQ">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDSU">March 7,</span> 2020</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=An+Internet+Pioneer+Ponders+the+Next+Revolution&amp;rft.date=1999-12-20&amp;rft.aulast=Markoff&amp;rft.aufirst=John&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.nytimes.com%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2Flibrary%2Ftech%2F99%2F12%2Fbiztech%2Farticles%2F122099outlook-bobb.html&amp;rfr_id=i