<li about="#cite_note-62" id="cite_note-62" data-mw-footnote-number="62"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDSc"><a href="#cite_ref-62" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDSg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDSk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-62" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt213" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDSo" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite conference","href":"./Template:Cite_conference"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Roberts"},"first1":{"wt":"Larry"},"last2":{"wt":"Marrill"},"first2":{"wt":"Tom"},"date":{"wt":"October 1966"},"title":{"wt":"Toward a Cooperative Network of Time-Shared Computers"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.packet.cc/files/toward-coop-net.html"},"conference":{"wt":"Fall AFIPS Conference"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20020401051508/http://www.packet.cc/files/toward-coop-net.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"2002-04-01"},"access-date":{"wt":"2017-09-10"},"author-link1":{"wt":"Lawrence Roberts (scientist)"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRobertsMarrill1966" class="citation conference cs1" about="#mwt213"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawrence_Roberts_(scientist)" title="Lawrence Roberts (scientist)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDSs">Roberts, Larry</a>; Marrill, Tom (October 1966). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20020401051508/http://www.packet.cc/files/toward-coop-net.html" class="external text" id="mwDSw"><i id="mwDS0">Toward a Cooperative Network of Time-Shared Computers</i></a>. Fall AFIPS Conference. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.packet.cc/files/toward-coop-net.html" class="external text" id="mwDS4">the original</a> on April 1, 2002<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDS8">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDTA">September 10,</span> 2017</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=conference&amp;rft.btitle=Toward+a+Cooperative+Network+of+Time-Shared+Computers&amp;rft.date=1966-10&amp;rft.aulast=Roberts&amp;rft.aufirst=Larry&amp;rft.au=Marrill%2C+Tom&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.packet.cc%2Ffiles%2Ftoward-coop-net.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt213" id="mwDTE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-63" id="cite_note-63" data-mw-footnote-number="63"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDTI"><a href="#cite_ref-63" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDTM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDTQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-63" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt216" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDTU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.forbes.com/sites/gilpress/2015/01/02/a-very-short-history-of-the-internet-and-the-web-2/"},"title":{"wt":"A Very Short History Of The Internet And The Web"},"last":{"wt":"Press"},"first":{"wt":"Gil"},"date":{"wt":"January 2, 2015"},"website":{"wt":"Forbes"},"language":{"wt":"en"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20150109145400/https://www.forbes.com/sites/gilpress/2015/01/02/a-very-short-history-of-the-internet-and-the-web-2/"},"archive-date":{"wt":"January 9, 2015"},"access-date":{"wt":"2020-02-07"},"quote":{"wt":"Roberts&apos; proposal that all host computers would connect to one another directly ... was not endorsed ... Wesley Clark ... suggested to Roberts that the network be managed by identical small computers, each attached to a host computer. Accepting the idea, Roberts named the small computers dedicated to network administration &apos;Interface Message Processors&apos; (IMPs), which later evolved into today&apos;s routers."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFPress2015" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt216">Press, Gil (January 2, 2015). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/gilpress/2015/01/02/a-very-short-history-of-the-internet-and-the-web-2/" class="external text" id="mwDTY">"A Very Short History Of The Internet And The Web"</a>. <i id="mwDTc">Forbes</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20150109145400/https://www.forbes.com/sites/gilpress/2015/01/02/a-very-short-history-of-the-internet-and-the-web-2/" class="external text" id="mwDTg">Archived</a> from the original on January 9, 2015<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDTk">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDTo">February 7,</span> 2020</span>. <q id="mwDTs">Roberts' proposal that all host computers would connect to one another directly ... was not endorsed ... Wesley Clark ... suggested to Roberts that the network be managed by identical small computers, each attached to a host computer. Accepting the idea, Roberts named the small computers dedicated to network administration 'Interface Message Processors' (IMPs), which later evolved into today's routers.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Forbes&amp;rft.atitle=A+Very+Short+History+Of+The+Internet+And+The+Web&amp;rft.date=2015-01-02&amp;rft.aulast=Press&amp;rft.aufirst=Gil&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.forbes.com%2Fsites%2Fgilpress%2F2015%2F01%2F02%2Fa-very-short-history-of-the-internet-and-the-web-2%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt216" id="mwDTw"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-64" id="cite_note-64" data-mw-footnote-number="64"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDT0"><a href="#cite_ref-64" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDT4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDT8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-64" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt219" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDUA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Citation ","href":"./Template:Citation"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://web.stanford.edu/dept/SUL/library/extra4/sloan/mousesite/EngelbartPapers/B1_F20_CompuMtg.html"},"title":{"wt":"SRI Project 5890-1; Networking (Reports on Meetings)"},"year":{"wt":"1967"},"publisher":{"wt":"Stanford University"},"access-date":{"wt":"2020-02-15"},"quote":{"wt":"W. Clark&apos;s message switching proposal (appended to Taylor&apos;s letter of April 24, 1967 to Engelbart)were reviewed."},"archive-date":{"wt":"February 2, 2020"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200202062940/https://web.stanford.edu/dept/SUL/library/extra4/sloan/mousesite/EngelbartPapers/B1_F20_CompuMtg.html"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation cs2" about="#mwt219" id="mwDUE"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20200202062940/https://web.stanford.edu/dept/SUL/library/extra4/sloan/mousesite/EngelbartPapers/B1_F20_CompuMtg.html" class="external text" id="mwDUI"><i id="mwDUM">SRI Project 5890-1; Networking (Reports on Meetings)</i></a>, Stanford University, 1967, archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.stanford.edu/dept/SUL/library/extra4/sloan/mousesite/EngelbartPapers/B1_F20_CompuMtg.html" class="external text" id="mwDUQ">the original</a> on February 2, 2020<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDUU">, retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDUY">February 15,</span> 2020</span>, <q id="mwDUc">W. Clark's message switching proposal (appended to Taylor's letter of April 24, 1967 to Engelbart)were reviewed.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=SRI+Project+5890-1%3B+Networking+%28Reports+on+Meetings%29&amp;rft.pub=Stanford+University&amp;rft.date=1967&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fweb.stanford.edu%2Fdept%2FSUL%2Flibrary%2Fextra4%2Fsloan%2Fmousesite%2FEngelbartPapers%2FB1_F20_CompuMtg.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt219" id="mwDUg"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-65" id="cite_note-65" data-mw-footnote-number="65"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDUk"><a href="#cite_ref-65" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDUo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDUs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-65" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt222" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDUw" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Roberts"},"first":{"wt":"Lawrence"},"date":{"wt":"1967"},"title":{"wt":"Multiple Computer Networks and Intercomputer Communications"},"chapter-url":{"wt":"https://people.mpi-sws.org/~gummadi/teaching/sp07/sys_seminar/arpanet.pdf"},"pages":{"wt":"3.1–3.6"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1145/800001.811680"},"quote":{"wt":"Thus the set of IMP&apos;s, plus the telephone lines and data sets would constitute a message switching network"},"chapter":{"wt":"Multiple computer networks and intercomputer communication"},"s2cid":{"wt":"17409102"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRoberts1967" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt222">Roberts, Lawrence (1967). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://people.mpi-sws.org/~gummadi/teaching/sp07/sys_seminar/arpanet.pdf" class="external text" id="mwDU0">"Multiple computer networks and intercomputer communication"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwDU4">(PDF)</span>. <i id="mwDU8">Multiple Computer Networks and Intercomputer Communications</i>. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDVA"> </span><span class="nowrap" id="mwDVE">3.1 –</span> <span class="nowrap" id="mwDVI">3.6</span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDVM">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1145%2F800001.811680" class="external text" id="mwDVQ">10.1145/800001.811680</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)" title="S2CID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDVU">S2CID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDVY"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:17409102" class="external text" id="mwDVc">17409102</a>. <q id="mwDVg">Thus the set of IMP's, plus the telephone lines and data sets would constitute a message switching network</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Multiple+computer+networks+and+intercomputer+communication&amp;rft.btitle=Multiple+Computer+Networks+and+Intercomputer+Communications&amp;rft.pages=3.1+-+3.6&amp;rft.date=1967&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1145%2F800001.811680&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A17409102%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft.aulast=Roberts&amp;rft.aufirst=Lawrence&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fpeople.mpi-sws.org%2F~gummadi%2Fteaching%2Fsp07%2Fsys_seminar%2Farpanet.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt222" id="mwDVk"></span></span></li>
