<li about="#cite_note-:9-80" id="cite_note-:9-80" data-mw-footnote-number="80"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDfU"><a href="#cite_ref-:9_80-0" id="mwDfY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDfc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-:9_80-1" id="mwDfg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDfk">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:9-80" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt483" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDfo" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Kirstein"},"first1":{"wt":"P.T."},"title":{"wt":"Early experiences with the Arpanet and Internet in the United Kingdom"},"journal":{"wt":"IEEE Annals of the History of Computing"},"date":{"wt":"1999"},"volume":{"wt":"21"},"issue":{"wt":"1"},"pages":{"wt":"38–44"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1109/85.759368"},"bibcode":{"wt":"1999IAHC...21a..38K"},"s2cid":{"wt":"1558618"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFKirstein1999" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt483">Kirstein, P.T. (1999). "Early experiences with the Arpanet and Internet in the United Kingdom". <i id="mwDfs">IEEE Annals of the History of Computing</i>. <b id="mwDfw">21</b> (1): <span class="nowrap" id="mwDf0">38–</span>44. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibcode_(identifier)" title="Bibcode (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDf4">Bibcode</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1999IAHC...21a..38K" class="external text" id="mwDf8">1999IAHC...21a..38K</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDgA">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1109%2F85.759368" class="external text" id="mwDgE">10.1109/85.759368</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)" title="S2CID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDgI">S2CID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDgM"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:1558618" class="external text" id="mwDgQ">1558618</a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=IEEE+Annals+of+the+History+of+Computing&amp;rft.atitle=Early+experiences+with+the+Arpanet+and+Internet+in+the+United+Kingdom&amp;rft.volume=21&amp;rft.issue=1&amp;rft.pages=38-44&amp;rft.date=1999&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A1558618%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1109%2F85.759368&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F1999IAHC...21a..38K&amp;rft.aulast=Kirstein&amp;rft.aufirst=P.T.&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt483" id="mwDgU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:122-81" id="cite_note-:122-81" data-mw-footnote-number="81"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDgY"><a href="#cite_ref-:122_81-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDgc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDgg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:122-81" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt273" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDgk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite thesis ","href":"./Template:Cite_thesis"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Clarke"},"first":{"wt":"Peter"},"title":{"wt":"Packet and circuit-switched data networks"},"date":{"wt":"1982"},"access-date":{"wt":"2024-01-21"},"degree":{"wt":"PhD"},"publisher":{"wt":"Department of Electrical Engineering, Imperial College of Science and Technology, University of London"},"url":{"wt":"https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/bitstream/10044/1/35864/2/Clarke-PN-1982-PhD-Thesis.pdf"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220803035935/https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/bitstream/10044/1/35864/2/Clarke-PN-1982-PhD-Thesis.pdf"},"archive-date":{"wt":"2022-08-03"},"url-status":{"wt":"dead"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwDgo" class="citation thesis cs1" about="#mwt273" data-x-id="CITEREFClarke1982">Clarke, Peter (1982). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20220803035935/https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/bitstream/10044/1/35864/2/Clarke-PN-1982-PhD-Thesis.pdf" class="external text" id="mwDgs"><i id="mwDgw">Packet and circuit-switched data networks</i></a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwDg0">(PDF)</span> (PhD thesis). Department of Electrical Engineering, Imperial College of Science and Technology, University of London. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://spiral.imperial.ac.uk/bitstream/10044/1/35864/2/Clarke-PN-1982-PhD-Thesis.pdf" class="external text" id="mwDg4">the original</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwDg8">(PDF)</span> on August 3, 2022<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDhA">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDhE">January 21,</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Adissertation&amp;rft.title=Packet+and+circuit-switched+data+networks&amp;rft.degree=PhD&amp;rft.inst=Department+of+Electrical+Engineering%2C+Imperial+College+of+Science+and+Technology%2C+University+of+London&amp;rft.date=1982&amp;rft.aulast=Clarke&amp;rft.aufirst=Peter&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fspiral.imperial.ac.uk%2Fbitstream%2F10044%2F1%2F35864%2F2%2FClarke-PN-1982-PhD-Thesis.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt273" id="mwDhI"></span>  "Many of the theoretical studies of the performance and design of the ARPA Network were developments of earlier work by Kleinrock ... Although these works concerned message switching networks, they were the basis for a lot of the ARPA network investigations ... The intention of the work of Kleinrock [in 1961] was to analyse the performance of store and forward networks ... Kleinrock [in 1970] extended the theoretical approaches of [his 1961 work] to the early ARPA network."</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-82" id="cite_note-82" data-mw-footnote-number="82"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDhM"><a href="#cite_ref-82" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDhQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDhU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-82" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt276" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDhY" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Postel"},"first":{"wt":"J."},"date":{"wt":"7 February 1979"},"title":{"wt":"Internet Meeting Notes -- 25 &amp; 26 January 1979"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/ien/ien76.pdf"},"access-date":{"wt":"9 February 2022"},"page":{"wt":"5"},"quote":{"wt":"Vint noted that UCLA&apos;s internet work is primarily theoretical research on throughput and delay analysis. This work is headed by L. Kleinrock."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFPostel1979" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt276">Postel, J. (February 7, 1979). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/ien/ien76.pdf" class="external text" id="mwDhc">"Internet Meeting Notes -- 25 &amp; 26 January 1979"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwDhg">(PDF)</span>. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDhk"> </span>5<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDho">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDhs">February 9,</span> 2022</span>. <q id="mwDhw">Vint noted that UCLA's internet work is primarily theoretical research on throughput and delay analysis. This work is headed by L. Kleinrock.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Internet+Meeting+Notes+--+25+%26+26+January+1979&amp;rft.pages=5&amp;rft.date=1979-02-07&amp;rft.aulast=Postel&amp;rft.aufirst=J.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rfc-editor.org%2Fien%2Fien76.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt276" id="mwDh0"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:43-83" id="cite_note-:43-83" data-mw-footnote-number="83"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDh4"><a href="#cite_ref-:43_83-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDh8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDiA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:43-83" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt279" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDiE" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Davies"},"first":{"wt":"Donald Watts"},"url":{"wt":"https://archive.org/details/computernetworks00davi/page/86/mode/2up?q=kleinrock+kleinrock%27s"},"title":{"wt":"Computer networks and their protocols"},"date":{"wt":"1979"},"publisher":{"wt":"Wiley"},"others":{"wt":"Internet Archive"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-471-99750-4"},"pages":{"wt":"See page refs highlighted at url"},"quote":{"wt":"In mathematical modelling use is made of the theories of queueing processes and of flows in networks, describing the performance of the network in a set of equations. ... The analytic method has been used with success by Kleinrock and others, but only if important simplifying assumptions are made. ... It is heartening in Kleinrock&apos;s work to see the good correspondence achieved between the results of analytic methods and those of simulation."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFDavies1979" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt279">Davies, Donald Watts (1979). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://archive.org/details/computernetworks00davi/page/86/mode/2up?q=kleinrock+kleinrock%27s" class="external text" id="mwDiI"><i id="mwDiM">Computer networks and their protocols</i></a>. Internet Archive. Wiley. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDiQ"> </span>See page refs highlighted at url. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDiU">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDiY"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-471-99750-4" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-471-99750-4" id="mwDic"><bdi id="mwDig">978-0-471-99750-4</bdi></a>. <q id="mwDik">In mathematical modelling use is made of the theories of queueing processes and of flows in networks, describing the performance of the network in a set of equations. ... The analytic method has been used with success by Kleinrock and others, but only if important simplifying assumptions are made. ... It is heartening in Kleinrock's work to see the good correspondence achieved between the results of analytic methods and those of simulation.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Computer+networks+and+their+protocols&amp;rft.pages=See+page+refs+highlighted+at+url&amp;rft.pub=Wiley&amp;rft.date=1979&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-471-99750-4&amp;rft.aulast=Davies&amp;rft.aufirst=Donald+Watts&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.org%2Fdetails%2Fcomputernetworks00davi%2Fpage%2F86%2Fmode%2F2up%3Fq%3Dkleinrock%2Bkleinrock%2527s&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt279" id="mwDio"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-84" id="cite_note-84" data-mw-footnote-number="84"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDis"><a href="#cite_ref-84" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDiw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDi0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-84" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt282" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDi4" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=7XAZnpCfQnEC&amp;q=1981+213+arpanet+hosts&amp;pg=PT289"},"title":{"wt":"Communication Technology Update and Fundamentals"},"last1":{"wt":"Grant"},"first1":{"wt":"August E."},"last2":{"wt":"Meadows"},"first2":{"wt":"Jennifer E."},"place":{"wt":"Burlington, Massachusetts"},"publisher":{"wt":"Focal Press"},"year":{"wt":"2008"},"edition":{"wt":"11th"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-240-81062-1"},"page":{"wt":"289"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFGrantMeadows2008" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt282">Grant, August E.; Meadows, Jennifer E. (2008). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=7XAZnpCfQnEC&amp;q=1981+213+arpanet+hosts&amp;pg=PT289" class="external text" id="mwDi8"><i id="mwDjA">Communication Technology Update and Fundamentals</i></a> (11th<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDjE"> </span>ed.). Burlington, Massachusetts: Focal Press. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDjI"> </span>289. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDjM">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDjQ"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-240-81062-1" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-240-81062-1" id="mwDjU"><bdi id="mwDjY">978-0-240-81062-1</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Communication+Technology+Update+and+Fundamentals&amp;rft.place=Burlington%2C+Massachusetts&amp;rft.pages=289&amp;rft.edition=11th&amp;rft.pub=Focal+Press&amp;rft.date=2008&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-240-81062-1&amp;rft.aulast=Grant&amp;rft.aufirst=August+E.&amp;rft.au=Meadows%2C+Jennifer+E.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3D7XAZnpCfQnEC%26q%3D1981%2B213%2Barpanet%2Bhosts%26pg%3DPT289&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt282" id="mwDjc"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:34-85" id="cite_note-:34-85" data-mw-footnote-number="85"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDjg"><a href="#cite_ref-:34_85-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDjk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDjo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:34-85" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt287" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDjs" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Russell"},"first1":{"wt":"Andrew L."},"last2":{"wt":"Schafer"},"first2":{"wt":"Valérie"},"date":{"wt":"2014"},"title":{"wt":"In the Shadow of ARPANET and Internet: Louis Pouzin and the Cyclades Network in the 1970s"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.jstor.org/stable/24468474"},"journal":{"wt":"Technology and Culture"},"volume":{"wt":"55"},"issue":{"wt":"4"},"pages":{"wt":"880–907"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1353/tech.2014.0096"},"issn":{"wt":"0040-165X"},"jstor":{"wt":"24468474"},"url-access":{"wt":"subscription"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRussellSchafer2014" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt287">Russell, Andrew L.; Schafer, Valérie (2014). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwDjw"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/24468474" class="external text" id="mwDj0">"In the Shadow of ARPANET and Internet: Louis Pouzin and the Cyclades Network in the 1970s"</a></span>. <i id="mwDj4">Technology and Culture</i>. <b id="mwDj8">55</b> (4): <span class="nowrap" id="mwDkA">880–</span>907. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDkE">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1353%2Ftech.2014.0096" class="external text" id="mwDkI">10.1353/tech.2014.0096</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDkM">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDkQ"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0040-165X" class="external text" id="mwDkU">0040-165X</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSTOR_(identifier)" title="JSTOR (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDkY">JSTOR</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDkc"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/24468474" class="external text" id="mwDkg">24468474</a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Technology+and+Culture&amp;rft.atitle=In+the+Shadow+of+ARPANET+and+Internet%3A+Louis+Pouzin+and+the+Cyclades+Network+in+the+1970s&amp;rft.volume=55&amp;rft.issue=4&amp;rft.pages=880-907&amp;rft.date=2014&amp;rft.issn=0040-165X&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.jstor.org%2Fstable%2F24468474%23id-name%3DJSTOR&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1353%2Ftech.2014.0096&amp;rft.aulast=Russell&amp;rft.aufirst=Andrew+L.&amp;rft.au=Schafer%2C+Val%C3%A9rie&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.jstor.org%2Fstable%2F24468474&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt287" id="mwDkk"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Pelkey2-86" id="cite_note-Pelkey2-86" data-mw-footnote-number="86"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDko"><a href="#cite_ref-Pelkey2_86-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDks"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDkw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pelkey2-86" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt290" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDk0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Pelkey"},"first":{"wt":"James"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.historyofcomputercommunications.info/Book/6/6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html"},"title":{"wt":"Entrepreneurial Capitalism and Innovation: A History of Computer Communications 1968-1988"},"chapter":{"wt":"6.3 CYCLADES Network and Louis Pouzin 1971-1972"},"quote":{"wt":"The inspiration for datagrams had two sources. One was Donald Davies&apos; studies."},"access-date":{"wt":"2021-11-21"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210617093154/https://www.historyofcomputercommunications.info/Book/6/6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"2021-06-17"},"url-status":{"wt":"dead"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwDk4" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt290" data-x-id="CITEREFPelkey">Pelkey, James. "6.3 CYCLADES Network and Louis Pouzin 1971-1972". <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20210617093154/https://www.historyofcomputercommunications.info/Book/6/6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html" class="external text" id="mwDk8"><i id="mwDlA">Entrepreneurial Capitalism and Innovation: A History of Computer Communications 1968-1988</i></a>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.historyofcomputercommunications.info/Book/6/6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html" class="external text" id="mwDlE">the original</a> on June 17, 2021<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDlI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDlM">November 21,</span> 2021</span>. <q id="mwDlQ">The inspiration for datagrams had two sources. One was Donald Davies' studies.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=6.3+CYCLADES+Network+and+Louis+Pouzin+1971-1972&amp;rft.btitle=Entrepreneurial+Capitalism+and+Innovation%3A+A+History+of+Computer+Communications+1968-1988&amp;rft.aulast=Pelkey&amp;rft.aufirst=James&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.historyofcomputercommunications.info%2FBook%2F6%2F6.3-CYCLADESNetworkLouisPouzin1-72.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt290" id="mwDlU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-87" id="cite_note-87" data-mw-footnote-number="87"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDlY"><a href="#cite_ref-87" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDlc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDlg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-87" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt293" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDlk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"A Technical History of CYCLADES"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.cs.utexas.edu/users/chris/think/Cyclades/index.shtml"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20130901092641/http://www.cs.utexas.edu/users/chris/think/Cyclades/index.shtml"},"archive-date":{"wt":"September 1, 2013"},"work":{"wt":"Technical Histories of the Internet &amp; other Network Protocols"},"publisher":{"wt":"Computer Science Department, University of Texas Austin"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt293" id="mwDlo"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20130901092641/http://www.cs.utexas.edu/users/chris/think/Cyclades/index.shtml" class="external text" id="mwDls">"A Technical History of CYCLADES"</a>. <i id="mwDlw">Technical Histories of the Internet &amp; other Network Protocols</i>. Computer Science Department, University of Texas Austin. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.cs.utexas.edu/users/chris/think/Cyclades/index.shtml" class="external text" id="mwDl0">the original</a> on September 1, 2013.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Technical+Histories+of+the+Internet+%26+other+Network+Protocols&amp;rft.atitle=A+Technical+History+of+CYCLADES&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.cs.utexas.edu%2Fusers%2Fchris%2Fthink%2FCyclades%2Findex.shtml&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt293" id="mwDl4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-88" id="cite_note-88" data-mw-footnote-number="88"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDl8"><a href="#cite_ref-88" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDmA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDmE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-88" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><i id="mwDmI">A Proposal for Interconnecting Packet Switching Networks</i>, L. Pouzin, Proceedings of EUROCOMP, Brunel University, May 1974, pp. 1023-36.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Green_2010_31-89" id="cite_note-Green_2010_31-89" data-mw-footnote-number="89"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDmM"><a href="#cite_ref-Green_2010_31_89-0" id="mwDmQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDmU">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Green_2010_31_89-1" id="mwDmY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDmc">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Green_2010_31-89" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt297" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDmg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Green"},"first":{"wt":"Lelia"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.worldcat.org/title/504280762"},"title":{"wt":"The internet: an introduction to new media"},"date":{"wt":"2010"},"publisher":{"wt":"Berg"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-1-84788-299-8"},"series":{"wt":"Berg new media series"},"page":{"wt":"31"},"oclc":{"wt":"504280762"},"quote":{"wt":"The original ARPANET design had made data integrity part of the IMP&apos;s store-and-forward role, but Cyclades end-to-end protocol greatly simplified the packet switching operations of the network. ... The idea was to adopt several principles from Cyclades and invert the ARPANET model to minimise international differences."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFGreen2010" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt297">Green, Lelia (2010). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.worldcat.org/title/504280762" class="external text" id="mwDmk"><i id="mwDmo">The internet: an introduction to new media</i></a>. Berg new media series. Berg. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDms"> </span>31. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDmw">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDm0"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-1-84788-299-8" title="Special:BookSources/978-1-84788-299-8" id="mwDm4"><bdi id="mwDm8">978-1-84788-299-8</bdi></a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OCLC_(identifier)" title="OCLC (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDnA">OCLC</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDnE"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/oclc/504280762" class="external text" id="mwDnI">504280762</a>. <q id="mwDnM">The original ARPANET design had made data integrity part of the IMP's store-and-forward role, but Cyclades end-to-end protocol greatly simplified the packet switching operations of the network. ... The idea was to adopt several principles from Cyclades and invert the ARPANET model to minimise international differences.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=The+internet%3A+an+introduction+to+new+media&amp;rft.series=Berg+new+media+series&amp;rft.pages=31&amp;rft.pub=Berg&amp;rft.date=2010&amp;rft_id=info%3Aoclcnum%2F504280762&amp;rft.isbn=978-1-84788-299-8&amp;rft.aulast=Green&amp;rft.aufirst=Lelia&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.worldcat.org%2Ftitle%2F504280762&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt297" id="mwDnQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Bennett20092-90" id="cite_note-Bennett20092-90" data-mw-footnote-number="90"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDnU"><a href="#cite_ref-Bennett20092_90-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDnY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDnc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bennett20092-90" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt300" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDng" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Bennett"},"first1":{"wt":"Richard"},"date":{"wt":"September 2009"},"title":{"wt":"Designed for Change: End-to-End Arguments, Internet Innovation, and the Net Neutrality Debate"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.itif.org/files/2009-designed-for-change.pdf"},"access-date":{"wt":"11 September 2017"},"publisher":{"wt":"Information Technology and Innovation Foundation"},"pages":{"wt":"7, 9, 11"},"quote":{"wt":"Two significant packet networks preceded the TCP/IP Internet: ARPANET and CYCLADES. The designers of the Internet borrowed heavily from these systems, especially CYCLADES ...  The first end-to-end research network was CYCLA DES, designed by Louis Pouzin at IRIA in France with the support of BBN’s Dave Walden and Alex McKenzie and deployed beginning in 1972."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFBennett2009" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt300">Bennett, Richard (September 2009). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.itif.org/files/2009-designed-for-change.pdf" class="external text" id="mwDnk">"Designed for Change: End-to-End Arguments, Internet Innovation, and the Net Neutrality Debate"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwDno">(PDF)</span>. Information Technology and Innovation Foundation. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDns"> </span>7, 9, 11<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDnw">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDn0">September 11,</span> 2017</span>. <q id="mwDn4">Two significant packet networks preceded the TCP/IP Internet: ARPANET and CYCLADES. The designers of the Internet borrowed heavily from these systems, especially CYCLADES ...  The first end-to-end research network was CYCLA DES, designed by Louis Pouzin at IRIA in France with the support of BBN's Dave Walden and Alex McKenzie and deployed beginning in 1972.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Designed+for+Change%3A+End-to-End+Arguments%2C+Internet+Innovation%2C+and+the+Net+Neutrality+Debate&amp;rft.pages=7%2C+9%2C+11&amp;rft.pub=Information+Technology+and+Innovation+Foundation&amp;rft.date=2009-09&amp;rft.aulast=Bennett&amp;rft.aufirst=Richard&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.itif.org%2Ffiles%2F2009-designed-for-change.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt300" id="mwDn8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:7-91" id="cite_note-:7-91" data-mw-footnote-number="91"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDoA"><a href="#cite_ref-:7_91-0" id="mwDoE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDoI">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-:7_91-1" id="mwDoM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDoQ">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:7-91" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt373" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDoU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Cerf"},"first1":{"wt":"V."},"last2":{"wt":"Kahn"},"first2":{"wt":"R."},"title":{"wt":"A Protocol for Packet Network Intercommunication"},"journal":{"wt":"IEEE Transactions on Communications"},"date":{"wt":"May 1974"},"volume":{"wt":"22"},"issue":{"wt":"5"},"pages":{"wt":"637–648"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1109/TCOM.1974.1092259"},"bibcode":{"wt":"1974ITCom..22..637C"},"quote":{"wt":"The authors wish to thank a number of colleagues for helpful comments during early discussions of international network protocols, especially R. Metcalfe, R. Scantlebury, D. Walden, and H. Zimmerman; D. Davies and L. Pouzin who constructively commented on the fragmentation and accounting issues; and S. Crocker who commented on the creation and destruction of associations."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFCerfKahn1974" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt373">Cerf, V.; Kahn, R. (May 1974). "A Protocol for Packet Network Intercommunication". <i id="mwDoY">IEEE Transactions on Communications</i>. <b id="mwDoc">22</b> (5): <span class="nowrap" id="mwDog">637–</span>648. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibcode_(identifier)" title="Bibcode (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDok">Bibcode</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1974ITCom..22..637C" class="external text" id="mwDoo">1974ITCom..22..637C</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDos">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1109%2FTCOM.1974.1092259" class="external text" id="mwDow">10.1109/TCOM.1974.1092259</a>. <q id="mwDo0">The authors wish to thank a number of colleagues for helpful comments during early discussions of international network protocols, especially R. Metcalfe, R. Scantlebury, D. Walden, and H. Zimmerman; D. Davies and L. Pouzin who constructively commented on the fragmentation and accounting issues; and S. Crocker who commented on the creation and destruction of associations.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=IEEE+Transactions+on+Communications&amp;rft.atitle=A+Protocol+for+Packet+Network+Intercommunication&amp;rft.volume=22&amp;rft.issue=5&amp;rft.pages=637-648&amp;rft.date=1974-05&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1109%2FTCOM.1974.1092259&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F1974ITCom..22..637C&amp;rft.aulast=Cerf&amp;rft.aufirst=V.&amp;rft.au=Kahn%2C+R.&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt373" id="mwDo4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-RFC_675-92" id="cite_note-RFC_675-92" data-mw-footnote-number="92"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDo8"><a href="#cite_ref-RFC_675_92-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDpA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDpE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-RFC_675-92" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt304" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDpI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite IETF","href":"./Template:Cite_IETF"},"params":{"rfc":{"wt":"675"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation cs1" about="#mwt304" id="mwDpM"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc675" class="external text" id="mwDpQ"><i id="mwDpU">RFC 675</i></a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Engineering_Task_Force" title="Internet Engineering Task Force" id="mwDpY">IETF</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDpc">doi</a>:<span class="id-lock-free" title="Freely accessible" id="mwDpg"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.17487%2FRFC0675" class="external text" id="mwDpk">10.17487/RFC0675</a></span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=RFC+675&amp;rft.pub=IETF&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.17487%2FRFC0675&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rfc-editor.org%2Frfc%2Frfc675&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt304" id="mwDpo"></span>" In the early phases of the design work, R. Metcalfe, A. McKenzie, H. Zimmerman, G. LeLann, and M. Elie were most helpful in explicating the various issues to be resolved."</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:8-93" id="cite_note-:8-93" data-mw-footnote-number="93"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDps"><a href="#cite_ref-:8_93-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDpw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDp0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:8-93" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt307" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDp4" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"2013-11-30"},"title":{"wt":"The internet&apos;s fifth man"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.economist.com/news/technology-quarterly/21590765-louis-pouzin-helped-create-internet-now-he-campaigning-ensure-its"},"access-date":{"wt":"2020-04-22"},"newspaper":{"wt":"The Economist"},"quote":{"wt":"In the early 1970s Mr Pouzin created an innovative data network that linked locations in France, Italy and Britain. Its simplicity and efficiency pointed the way to a network that could connect not just dozens of machines, but millions of them. It captured the imagination of Dr Cerf and Dr Kahn, who included aspects of its design in the protocols that now power the internet."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt307" id="mwDp8"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.economist.com/news/technology-quarterly/21590765-louis-pouzin-helped-create-internet-now-he-campaigning-ensure-its" class="external text" id="mwDqA">"The internet's fifth man"</a>. <i id="mwDqE">The Economist</i>. November 30, 2013<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDqI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDqM">April 22,</span> 2020</span>. <q id="mwDqQ">In the early 1970s Mr Pouzin created an innovative data network that linked locations in France, Italy and Britain. Its simplicity and efficiency pointed the way to a network that could connect not just dozens of machines, but millions of them. It captured the imagination of Dr Cerf and Dr Kahn, who included aspects of its design in the protocols that now power the internet.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Economist&amp;rft.atitle=The+internet%27s+fifth+man&amp;rft.date=2013-11-30&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.economist.com%2Fnews%2Ftechnology-quarterly%2F21590765-louis-pouzin-helped-create-internet-now-he-campaigning-ensure-its&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt307" id="mwDqU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-94" id="cite_note-94" data-mw-footnote-number="94"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDqY"><a href="#cite_ref-94" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDqc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDqg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-94" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt310" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDqk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Abbate"},"first":{"wt":"Janet"},"author-link":{"wt":"Janet Abbate"},"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=E2BdY6WQo4AC&amp;pg=PA125"},"title":{"wt":"Inventing the Internet"},"date":{"wt":"2000"},"publisher":{"wt":"MIT Press"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-262-51115-5"},"pages":{"wt":"125"},"language":{"wt":"en"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwDqo" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt310" data-x-id="CITEREFAbbate2000"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janet_Abbate" title="Janet Abbate" id="mwDqs">Abbate, Janet</a> (2000). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=E2BdY6WQo4AC&amp;pg=PA125" class="external text" id="mwDqw"><i id="mwDq0">Inventing the Internet</i></a>. MIT Press. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDq4"> </span>125. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDq8">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDrA"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-262-51115-5" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-262-51115-5" id="mwDrE"><bdi id="mwDrI">978-0-262-51115-5</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Inventing+the+Internet&amp;rft.pages=125&amp;rft.pub=MIT+Press&amp;rft.date=2000&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-262-51115-5&amp;rft.aulast=Abbate&amp;rft.aufirst=Janet&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3DE2BdY6WQo4AC%26pg%3DPA125&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt310" id="mwDrM"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:11-95" id="cite_note-:11-95" data-mw-footnote-number="95"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDrQ"><a href="#cite_ref-:11_95-0" id="mwDrU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDrY">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-:11_95-1" id="mwDrc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDrg">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:11-95" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt315" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDrk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Rybczynski"},"first":{"wt":"Tony"},"date":{"wt":"2009"},"title":{"wt":"Commercialization of packet switching (1975–1985): A Canadian perspective [History of Communications]"},"journal":{"wt":"IEEE Communications Magazine"},"volume":{"wt":"47"},"issue":{"wt":"12"},"pages":{"wt":"26–31"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1109/MCOM.2009.5350364"},"s2cid":{"wt":"23243636"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRybczynski2009" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt315">Rybczynski, Tony (2009). "Commercialization of packet switching (1975–1985): A Canadian perspective [History of Communications]". <i id="mwDro">IEEE Communications Magazine</i>. <b id="mwDrs">47</b> (12): <span class="nowrap" id="mwDrw">26–</span>31. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDr0">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1109%2FMCOM.2009.5350364" class="external text" id="mwDr4">10.1109/MCOM.2009.5350364</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)" title="S2CID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDr8">S2CID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDsA"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:23243636" class="external text" id="mwDsE">23243636</a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=IEEE+Communications+Magazine&amp;rft.atitle=Commercialization+of+packet+switching+%281975%E2%80%931985%29%3A+A+Canadian+perspective+%5BHistory+of+Communications%5D&amp;rft.volume=47&amp;rft.issue=12&amp;rft.pages=26-31&amp;rft.date=2009&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1109%2FMCOM.2009.5350364&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A23243636%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft.aulast=Rybczynski&amp;rft.aufirst=Tony&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt315" id="mwDsI"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:12-96" id="cite_note-:12-96" data-mw-footnote-number="96"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDsM"><a href="#cite_ref-:12_96-0" id="mwDsQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDsU">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-:12_96-1" id="mwDsY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDsc">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:12-96" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt318" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDsg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite journal","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Schwartz"},"first":{"wt":"Mischa"},"date":{"wt":"2010"},"title":{"wt":"X.25 Virtual Circuits - TRANSPAC IN France - Pre-Internet Data Networking [History of communications]"},"journal":{"wt":"IEEE Communications Magazine"},"volume":{"wt":"48"},"issue":{"wt":"11"},"pages":{"wt":"40–46"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1109/MCOM.2010.5621965"},"s2cid":{"wt":"23639680"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFSchwartz2010" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt318">Schwartz, Mischa (2010). "X.25 Virtual Circuits - TRANSPAC IN France - Pre-Internet Data Networking [History of communications]". <i id="mwDsk">IEEE Communications Magazine</i>. <b id="mwDso">48</b> (11): <span class="nowrap" id="mwDss">40–</span>46. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDsw">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1109%2FMCOM.2010.5621965" class="external text" id="mwDs0">10.1109/MCOM.2010.5621965</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)" title="S2CID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDs4">S2CID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDs8"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:23639680" class="external text" id="mwDtA">23639680</a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=IEEE+Communications+Magazine&amp;rft.atitle=X.25+Virtual+Circuits+-+TRANSPAC+IN+France+-+Pre-Internet+Data+Networking+%5BHistory+of+communications%5D&amp;rft.volume=48&amp;rft.issue=11&amp;rft.pages=40-46&amp;rft.date=2010&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1109%2FMCOM.2010.5621965&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A23639680%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft.aulast=Schwartz&amp;rft.aufirst=Mischa&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt318" id="mwDtE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-97" id="cite_note-97" data-mw-footnote-number="97"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDtI"><a href="#cite_ref-97" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDtM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDtQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-97" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt321" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDtU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"author":{"wt":"tsbedh"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.itu.int/ITU-T/studygroups/com17/history.html"},"title":{"wt":"History of X.25, CCITT Plenary Assemblies and Book Colors"},"publisher":{"wt":"Itu.int"},"access-date":{"wt":"June 5, 2009"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFtsbedh" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt321">tsbedh. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.itu.int/ITU-T/studygroups/com17/history.html" class="external text" id="mwDtY">"History of X.25, CCITT Plenary Assemblies and Book Colors"</a>. Itu.int<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDtc">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDtg">June 5,</span> 2009</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=History+of+X.25%2C+CCITT+Plenary+Assemblies+and+Book+Colors&amp;rft.pub=Itu.int&amp;rft.au=tsbedh&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.itu.int%2FITU-T%2Fstudygroups%2Fcom17%2Fhistory.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt321" id="mwDtk"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-98" id="cite_note-98" data-mw-footnote-number="98"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDto"><a href="#cite_ref-98" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDts"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDtw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-98" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt326" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDt0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"Events in British Telecomms History"},"work":{"wt":"Events in British TelecommsHistory"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.sigtel.com/tel_hist_brief.html"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20030405153523/http://www.sigtel.com/tel_hist_brief.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"April 5, 2003"},"access-date":{"wt":"November 25, 2005"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt326" id="mwDt4"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20030405153523/http://www.sigtel.com/tel_hist_brief.html" class="external text" id="mwDt8">"Events in British Telecomms History"</a>. <i id="mwDuA">Events in British TelecommsHistory</i>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.sigtel.com/tel_hist_brief.html" class="external text" id="mwDuE">the original</a> on April 5, 2003<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwDuI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwDuM">November 25,</span> 2005</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Events+in+British+TelecommsHistory&amp;rft.atitle=Events+in+British+Telecomms+History&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.sigtel.com%2Ftel_hist_brief.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt326" id="mwDuQ"></span></span></li>
