<li about="#cite_note-100" id="cite_note-100" data-mw-footnote-number="100"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDu0"><a href="#cite_ref-100" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDu4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDu8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-100" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt331" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwDvA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite thesis ","href":"./Template:Cite_thesis"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Ikram"},"first1":{"wt":"Nadeem"},"title":{"wt":"Internet Protocols and a Partial Implementation of CCITT X.75"},"date":{"wt":"1985"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.proquest.com/openview/678d6e16a1f0ac0470e12db67623ce91/1"},"page":{"wt":"2"},"quote":{"wt":"Two main approaches to internetworking have come into existence based upon the virtual circuit and the datagram services. The vast majority of the work on interconnecting networks falls into one of these two approaches: The CCITT X.75 Recommendation; The DoD Internet Protocol (IP)."},"id":{"wt":"{{OCLC|663449435|1091194379}}"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFIkram1985" class="citation thesis cs1" about="#mwt331">Ikram, Nadeem (1985). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.proquest.com/openview/678d6e16a1f0ac0470e12db67623ce91/1" class="external text" id="mwDvE"><i id="mwDvI">Internet Protocols and a Partial Implementation of CCITT X.75</i></a> (Thesis). p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDvM"> </span>2. <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt333" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwDvQ" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OCLC_(identifier)" title="OCLC (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDvU">OCLC</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDvY"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.worldcat.org/oclc/663449435" class="external text" id="mwDvc">663449435</a>, <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.worldcat.org/oclc/1091194379" class="external text" id="mwDvg">1091194379</a>. <q id="mwDvk">Two main approaches to internetworking have come into existence based upon the virtual circuit and the datagram services. The vast majority of the work on interconnecting networks falls into one of these two approaches: The CCITT X.75 Recommendation; The DoD Internet Protocol (IP).</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Adissertation&amp;rft.title=Internet+Protocols+and+a+Partial+Implementation+of+CCITT+X.75&amp;rft.date=1985&amp;rft.aulast=Ikram&amp;rft.aufirst=Nadeem&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.proquest.com%2Fopenview%2F678d6e16a1f0ac0470e12db67623ce91%2F1&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt331" id="mwDvo"></span></span></li>
