<li about="#cite_note-:5-109" id="cite_note-:5-109" data-mw-footnote-number="109"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwD10"><a href="#cite_ref-:5_109-0" id="mwD14"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD18">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-:5_109-1" id="mwD2A"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD2E">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:5-109" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt368" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwD2I" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Hauben"},"first":{"wt":"Ronda"},"year":{"wt":"2004"},"title":{"wt":"The Internet: On its International Origins and Collaborative Vision"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.ais.org/~jrh/acn/ACn12-2.a03.txt"},"journal":{"wt":"Amateur Computerist"},"volume":{"wt":"12"},"issue":{"wt":"2"},"access-date":{"wt":"May 29, 2009"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFHauben2004" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt368">Hauben, Ronda (2004). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.ais.org/~jrh/acn/ACn12-2.a03.txt" class="external text" id="mwD2M">"The Internet: On its International Origins and Collaborative Vision"</a>. <i id="mwD2Q">Amateur Computerist</i>. <b id="mwD2U">12</b> (2)<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwD2Y">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwD2c">May 29,</span> 2009</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Amateur+Computerist&amp;rft.atitle=The+Internet%3A+On+its+International+Origins+and+Collaborative+Vision&amp;rft.volume=12&amp;rft.issue=2&amp;rft.date=2004&amp;rft.aulast=Hauben&amp;rft.aufirst=Ronda&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ais.org%2F~jrh%2Facn%2FACn12-2.a03.txt&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt368" id="mwD2g"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-110" id="cite_note-110" data-mw-footnote-number="110"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwD2k"><a href="#cite_ref-110" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwD2o"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD2s">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-110" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt377" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwD2w" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"13 December 2013"},"title":{"wt":"The internet&apos;s fifth man"},"work":{"wt":"The Economist"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.economist.com/news/technology-quarterly/21590765-louis-pouzin-helped-create-internet-now-he-campaigning-ensure-its"},"access-date":{"wt":"11 September 2017"},"quote":{"wt":"In the early 1970s Mr Pouzin created an innovative data network that linked locations in France, Italy and Britain. Its simplicity and efficiency pointed the way to a network that could connect not just dozens of machines, but millions of them. It captured the imagination of Dr Cerf and Dr Kahn, who included aspects of its design in the protocols that now power the internet."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt377" id="mwD20"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.economist.com/news/technology-quarterly/21590765-louis-pouzin-helped-create-internet-now-he-campaigning-ensure-its" class="external text" id="mwD24">"The internet's fifth man"</a>. <i id="mwD28">The Economist</i>. December 13, 2013<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwD3A">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwD3E">September 11,</span> 2017</span>. <q id="mwD3I">In the early 1970s Mr Pouzin created an innovative data network that linked locations in France, Italy and Britain. Its simplicity and efficiency pointed the way to a network that could connect not just dozens of machines, but millions of them. It captured the imagination of Dr Cerf and Dr Kahn, who included aspects of its design in the protocols that now power the internet.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Economist&amp;rft.atitle=The+internet%27s+fifth+man&amp;rft.date=2013-12-13&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.economist.com%2Fnews%2Ftechnology-quarterly%2F21590765-louis-pouzin-helped-create-internet-now-he-campaigning-ensure-its&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt377" id="mwD3M"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-111" id="cite_note-111" data-mw-footnote-number="111"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwD3Q"><a href="#cite_ref-111" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwD3U"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD3Y">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-111" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt380" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwD3c" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite ietf ","href":"./Template:Cite_ietf"},"params":{"author1":{"wt":"[[Vint Cerf]]"},"author2":{"wt":"[[Yogen Dalal]]"},"author3":{"wt":"Carl Sunshine"},"date":{"wt":"December 1974"},"RFC":{"wt":"675"},"title":{"wt":"Specification of Internet Transmission Control Protocol"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFVint_CerfYogen_DalalCarl_Sunshine1974" class="citation cs1" about="#mwt380"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vint_Cerf" title="Vint Cerf" id="mwD3g">Vint Cerf</a>; <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yogen_Dalal" title="Yogen Dalal" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD3k">Yogen Dalal</a>; Carl Sunshine (December 1974). <i id="mwD3o">Specification of Internet Transmission Control Protocol</i>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Engineering_Task_Force" title="Internet Engineering Task Force" id="mwD3s">IETF</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RFC_(identifier)" title="RFC (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD3w">RFC</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwD30"> </span><span class="id-lock-free" title="Freely accessible" id="mwD34"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc675" class="external text" id="mwD38">675</a></span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Specification+of+Internet+Transmission+Control+Protocol&amp;rft.pub=IETF&amp;rft.date=1974-12&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Ftools.ietf.org%2Fhtml%2Frfc675%23id-name%3DRFC&amp;rft.au=Vint+Cerf&amp;rft.au=Yogen+Dalal&amp;rft.au=Carl+Sunshine&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt380" id="mwD4A"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-112" id="cite_note-112" data-mw-footnote-number="112"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwD4E"><a href="#cite_ref-112" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwD4I"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD4M">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-112" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt384" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwD4Q" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"http://www.computerhistory.org/about/press_relations/releases/20071101/"},"access-date":{"wt":"November 22, 2007"},"title":{"wt":"Computer History Museum and Web History Center Celebrate 30th Anniversary of Internet Milestone"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt384" id="mwD4U"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.computerhistory.org/about/press_relations/releases/20071101/" class="external text" id="mwD4Y">"Computer History Museum and Web History Center Celebrate 30th Anniversary of Internet Milestone"</a><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwD4c">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwD4g">November 22,</span> 2007</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Computer+History+Museum+and+Web+History+Center+Celebrate+30th+Anniversary+of+Internet+Milestone&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.computerhistory.org%2Fabout%2Fpress_relations%2Freleases%2F20071101%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt384" id="mwD4k"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-113" id="cite_note-113" data-mw-footnote-number="113"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwD4o"><a href="#cite_ref-113" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwD4s"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD4w">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-113" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt387" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwD40" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"http://news.cnet.com/Internet-van-helped-drive-evolution-of-the-Web/2100-1033_3-6217511.html"},"title":{"wt":"&apos;Internet van&apos; helped drive evolution of the Web"},"first":{"wt":"Erica"},"last":{"wt":"Ogg"},"work":{"wt":"[[CNET]]"},"date":{"wt":"2007-11-08"},"access-date":{"wt":"2011-11-12"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFOgg2007" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt387">Ogg, Erica (November 8, 2007). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://news.cnet.com/Internet-van-helped-drive-evolution-of-the-Web/2100-1033_3-6217511.html" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="http://news.cnet.com/Internet-van-helped-drive-evolution-of-the-Web/2100-1033_3-6217511.html" id="mwD44">"<span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwD48"></span>'Internet van' helped drive evolution of the Web"</a>. <i id="mwD5A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNET" title="CNET" id="mwD5E">CNET</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwD5I">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwD5M">November 12,</span> 2011</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=CNET&amp;rft.atitle=%27Internet+van%27+helped+drive+evolution+of+the+Web&amp;rft.date=2007-11-08&amp;rft.aulast=Ogg&amp;rft.aufirst=Erica&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fnews.cnet.com%2FInternet-van-helped-drive-evolution-of-the-Web%2F2100-1033_3-6217511.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt387" id="mwD5Q"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Panzaris-114" id="cite_note-Panzaris-114" data-mw-footnote-number="114"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwD5U"><a href="#cite_ref-Panzaris_114-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwD5Y"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD5c">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Panzaris-114" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt390" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwD5g" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Panzaris"},"first1":{"wt":"Georgios"},"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=9yMhAQAAIAAJ"},"title":{"wt":"Machines and romances: the technical and narrative construction of networked computing as a general-purpose platform, 1960–1995"},"date":{"wt":"2008"},"publisher":{"wt":"[[Stanford University]]"},"page":{"wt":"128"},"quote":{"wt":"Despite the misgivings of Xerox Corporation (which intended to make PUP the basis of a proprietary commercial networking product), researchers at Xerox PARC, including ARPANET pioneers Robert Metcalfe and Yogen Dalal, shared the basic contours of their research with colleagues at TCP and Internet working group meetings in 1976 and 1977, suggesting the possible benefits of separating TCPs routing and transmission control functions into two discrete layers."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFPanzaris2008" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt390">Panzaris, Georgios (2008). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=9yMhAQAAIAAJ" class="external text" id="mwD5k"><i id="mwD5o">Machines and romances: the technical and narrative construction of networked computing as a general-purpose platform, 1960–1995</i></a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanford_University" title="Stanford University" id="mwD5s">Stanford University</a>. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwD5w"> </span>128. <q id="mwD50">Despite the misgivings of Xerox Corporation (which intended to make PUP the basis of a proprietary commercial networking product), researchers at Xerox PARC, including ARPANET pioneers Robert Metcalfe and Yogen Dalal, shared the basic contours of their research with colleagues at TCP and Internet working group meetings in 1976 and 1977, suggesting the possible benefits of separating TCPs routing and transmission control functions into two discrete layers.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Machines+and+romances%3A+the+technical+and+narrative+construction+of+networked+computing+as+a+general-purpose+platform%2C+1960%E2%80%931995&amp;rft.pages=128&amp;rft.pub=Stanford+University&amp;rft.date=2008&amp;rft.aulast=Panzaris&amp;rft.aufirst=Georgios&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3D9yMhAQAAIAAJ&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt390" id="mwD54"></span></span></li>
