<li about="#cite_note-240" id="cite_note-240" data-mw-footnote-number="240"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFP8"><a href="#cite_ref-240" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFQA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFQE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-240" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt833" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwFQI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"USC/ICANN Transition Agreement"},"website":{"wt":"icann.org"},"date":{"wt":"14 May 2000"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.icann.org/en/general/usc-icann-transition-agreement.htm"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20081005055337/http://www.icann.org/en/general/usc-icann-transition-agreement.htm"},"archive-date":{"wt":"October 5, 2008"},"access-date":{"wt":"October 15, 2009"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt833" id="mwFQM"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20081005055337/http://www.icann.org/en/general/usc-icann-transition-agreement.htm" class="external text" id="mwFQQ">"USC/ICANN Transition Agreement"</a>. <i id="mwFQU">icann.org</i>. May 14, 2000. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.icann.org/en/general/usc-icann-transition-agreement.htm" class="external text" id="mwFQY">the original</a> on October 5, 2008<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwFQc">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwFQg">October 15,</span> 2009</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=icann.org&amp;rft.atitle=USC%2FICANN+Transition+Agreement&amp;rft.date=2000-05-14&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.icann.org%2Fen%2Fgeneral%2Fusc-icann-transition-agreement.htm&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt833" id="mwFQk"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-241" id="cite_note-241" data-mw-footnote-number="241"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFQo"><a href="#cite_ref-241" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFQs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFQw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-241" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt836" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwFQ0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Anderson"},"first":{"wt":"Nate"},"title":{"wt":"ICANN cuts cord to US government, gets broader oversight"},"website":{"wt":"Ars Technica"},"date":{"wt":"30 September 2009"},"url":{"wt":"https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2009/09/icann-cuts-cord-to-us-government-gets-broader-oversight/"},"quote":{"wt":"ICANN, which oversees the Internet&apos;s domain name system, is a private nonprofit that reports to the US Department of Commerce. Under a new agreement, that relationship will change, and ICANN&apos;s accountability goes global"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFAnderson2009" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt836">Anderson, Nate (September 30, 2009). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2009/09/icann-cuts-cord-to-us-government-gets-broader-oversight/" class="external text" id="mwFQ4">"ICANN cuts cord to US government, gets broader oversight"</a>. <i id="mwFQ8">Ars Technica</i>. <q id="mwFRA">ICANN, which oversees the Internet's domain name system, is a private nonprofit that reports to the US Department of Commerce. Under a new agreement, that relationship will change, and ICANN's accountability goes global</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Ars+Technica&amp;rft.atitle=ICANN+cuts+cord+to+US+government%2C+gets+broader+oversight&amp;rft.date=2009-09-30&amp;rft.aulast=Anderson&amp;rft.aufirst=Nate&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Farstechnica.com%2Ftech-policy%2F2009%2F09%2Ficann-cuts-cord-to-us-government-gets-broader-oversight%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+the+Internet" class="Z3988" about="#mwt836" id="mwFRE"></span></span></li>
